# ThalVital web-root hardening.
# The release layout uses docroot = release/public/ (the `git archive --prefix=public/`
# tree from scripts/release-tag.ps1), so the whole app — including schema.sql, seed.sql,
# docs, and includes/ — sits under the web root. Deny direct web access to everything
# that is not a real HTTP entry point.
#
# NOTE: .htaccess only applies if the vhost sets `AllowOverride FileInfo Limit` (or All).
# On a hardened shared box AllowOverride may be None, in which case these rules are
# IGNORED — the authoritative control is the equivalent <Directory> block in the Apache
# vhost (see DEPLOYMENT.md → "Apache vhost"). Keep both in sync; this file is defense-in-depth.

# 1) Never serve source data, docs, tooling, or config as static files.
<FilesMatch "\.(sql|md|ps1|sh|sample\.php|sock|log)$">
  Require all denied
</FilesMatch>
<Files "config.php">
  Require all denied
</Files>

# 2) Block internal PHP (require'd server-side, never fetched over HTTP) and tooling dirs.
RedirectMatch 404 ^/(includes|scripts)(/|$)

# 3) Never expose a VCS directory if one is ever present in a release.
RedirectMatch 404 ^/\.(git|hg|svn)(/|$)
